    LineComment "// Effects declare a function's interaction with the world, in its signature:"
    Newline "\n"
    LineComment "// io touches it, async suspends (consumed explicitly with await), nondet does"
    Newline "\n"
    LineComment "// not reproduce. No declaration means pure — evaluated at compile time and"
    Newline "\n"
    LineComment "// folded to a value, as every belt expression has been. An effectful function"
    Newline "\n"
    LineComment "// is never folded; it compiles to runtime code for a target."
    Newline "\n"
    Newline "\n"
    LineComment "// The root of an effect is a native the toolchain's registry supplies — here"
    Newline "\n"
    LineComment "// datetime.now(), the current instant: nondet, because a wall-clock read does"
    Newline "\n"
    LineComment "// not reproduce. A root cannot be declared in user code: nothing there could"
    Newline "\n"
    LineComment "// supply its implementation."
    Newline "\n"
    Newline "\n"
    LineComment "// Effects propagate by declaration, never by silent inference: stamp calls"
    Newline "\n"
    LineComment "// datetime.now(), so it must declare nondet itself. A nondet wrapper stays"
    Newline "\n"
    LineComment "// nondet — the timestamp must never fold into a value."
    Newline "\n"
